From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] home: AD5X default home layout

The ad5x preset gets a home seed (assets/config/panel_widgets/ad5x/home.json,
read by PanelWidgetConfig::load_preset_overlay) for the 800x480 panel's
grid only (medium@12x8; every other grid keeps the shipped defaults).
Top row: nozzle and bed temperature, fan speeds, notifications. Left:
print status, detailed (progress arc, file, layer, time left; a tap
opens the print screen with Pause/Tune/Cancel; the last print with
Reprint Last when idle), without the temperature row of its
detailed card. Right: the IFS slots (the spool slot, moved), Preheat
(PLA/PETG/ABS/TPU, Cool Down while heating) without its temperature
column and one track tall; under it the LED light (its own slot, so a
printer without a controllable light leaves the cell empty) and the
live Z offset (tap: Tune with baby steps); Motion (homing and jog) and
an "Unload" macro button for
UNLOAD_FILAMENT. Preheat/Cool Down and Unload are greyed and do nothing
while a print is printing or paused. printer_image, temp_graph and
tips are switched off there. A tap on a temperature still opens the
temperature graph.

print_status takes a new config key, show_temps (default true): false
hides the detailed active card's nozzle/bed/chamber row through the
print_status_temps_hidden subject. Only the seed sets it.

preheat may now be one track tall (registry min_rowspan 1, half rows):
its fits_at() asks for the button's height, so a grid whose track is
shorter (micro, tiny) grows it back to the whole cell. Tests that used
preheat as the fixed-row-span or half-on-one-axis example use
filament_buffer and control_buttons, or drop the one-axis case, which
no widget has any more.

The mock AD5X persona gets the printer's [led chamber_led].

New widget config keys, all off by default so other layouts keep
upstream behaviour:
- preheat show_temps (default true): false hides the nozzle/bed column
  beside the button.
- preheat and favorite_macro lock_while_printing (default false): while
  print_active is 1 (printing or paused) the button is drawn at 40%
  opacity and a tap only shows "Not available while printing". Opacity
  rather than LV_STATE_DISABLED, which the macro tile's XML already binds
  to the connection state.
- favorite_macro label: tile text in place of the macro's name, drawn
  whatever show_widget_labels says and kept while the glyph shrinks. The
  tile's name label now hides through its size verdict alone (which
  already reads show_widget_labels) instead of also binding the setting
  in XML. The config modal keeps the keys it does not edit.

A seed may carry a "revision", which joins the preset in the default
layout's signature. A home layout that is still the unedited default
(its stored hash matches) is re-resolved on the first READY populate
when the signature moves, so printers that never edited their home
screen move to this layout on update; an edited layout is left alone.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
---
